From 7bd0a753e5f5bf344b26417bce8fd6aac7f4e046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:29:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Restore VP9 8K encoding scalability workaround

Confirmed codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp is actually compiled into this
product's build (present in the regenerated Android.bp), so this
upstream-reported bug workaround (commit d4129e148,
https://github.com/intel/media-driver/issues/1847: VP9 8K encoding
with scalability enabled produces incorrect output) applies here and
was silently discarded by the overlay like the other fixes in this
series.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 .../agnostic/gen12/codec/hal/codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp         | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media_driver/agnostic/gen12/codec/hal/codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp b/media_driver/agnostic/gen12/codec/hal/codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp
index 428454062..4174ef06d 100644
--- a/media_driver/agnostic/gen12/codec/hal/codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp
+++ b/media_driver/agnostic/gen12/codec/hal/codechal_vdenc_vp9_g12.cpp
@@ -963,7 +963,7 @@ MOS_STATUS CodechalVdencVp9StateG12::GetSystemPipeNumberCommon()
         &userFeatureData,
         m_osInterface->pOsContext);
 
-    bool disableScalability = m_hwInterface->IsDisableScalability();
+    bool disableScalability = true; // m_hwInterface->IsDisableScalability();
     if (statusKey == MOS_STATUS_SUCCESS)
     {
         disableScalability = userFeatureData.i32Data ? true : false;
-- 
2.34.1

